 "description": "Benchmark task (docs/benchmark_rules.md). 5.08 GHz dual-tank (transformer) cross-coupled NMOS LC-VCO with a 4-bit cap bank, varactor fine tuning and an output buffer (paper Fig. 10), gpdk180, 0.85 V core, 1.8 V varactor bias / buffer drain (bias-T, 50 ohm per output), 27 C (not reported: G2). Conditions: nominal (cap-bank code 8, NN, 0.85 V) and the two extreme codes (label code15: all bank bits on, label code0: all off) for the tuning-range end points; the paper reports no PVT table (post-layout PN change < 3 dB, no corners given) and a supply drift only graphically (Fig. 15), so no further conditions. Phase noise at 100 kHz / 800 kHz / 10 MHz, FoM and power are taken at the Vc that gives 5.08 GHz (PSS tuning sweep, found per design). The measured nodes are the buffer outputs RFL / RFR (differential) with the bias-T and 50 ohm load as testbench elements; the start-up kick goes into the tank node XDUT.D1. Targets are the paper's measured values with 10 % linear tolerance. No Monte Carlo (none reported). G8 at the DC equilibrium (owner 2026-10-23 for LC oscillators), varactors / bank switches / control inverters excluded.",
 "source": {
  "doi": "10.1109/TCSI.2024.3443752",
  "title": "Lohrabi Pour, Ha, Nikpaik, 'An Ultra-Low Phase Noise Dual-Tank Oscillator Featuring Tank Impedance Scaling', IEEE TCAS-I 71(12):5657-5668, Dec 2024",
  "figure": "Fig. 10 (cross-coupled NMOS M1/M2, transformer Lp/Ls dual tank with Cs, Cp,f, Cp,s, varactor network, 4-bit capacitor bank, output + dummy buffers); element values Table III and Sec. IV"
 },
